// D1693's third floor — `operator '+'` over a nullable SCALAR narrowed at the use site. The
// list template covers index and `.length`; the operator refuses in its own words
// (`operator '+' is not defined for i32 | null and i32`) and needs its own value.
//
// Both narrowing spellings again, and the `??` one is the sharper: the operand's type after
// `?? 0` is `i32`, and the pin still named `i32 | null`.
//
// The `is_in_while` cell is SILENT at BOTH faces and on BOTH seeds — D1698, a `??` result
// stored into a box-typed local under a `while` narrowing. It needs no pin and no generic, so
// it is left graded rather than skipped: this row's close does not touch it either way.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: the builder already guards the read with `!= null`, so this TEST is a second null
compare on a value the first one narrowed — the refusal is the template's shape, not a floor
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mkN(): i32 | null { return 4 }
// @@VALUE@@
mkN()
// @@TYPE@@
i32 | null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v + 1)
const q = v ?? 0
print(q + 2)
